easy-going:
中：a. 随和的
英：a. Moving easily; hence, mild-tempered; ease-loving;
   inactive.

eleemosynarily:
中：adv. eleemosynary的变形
英：adv. In an eleemosynary manner; by charity;
   charitably.

elementariness:
中：n. elementary的变形
英：n. The state of being elementary; original simplicity;
   uncompounded state.

eligibleness:
中：n. eligible的变形
英：n. The quality worthy or qualified to be chosen;
   suitableness; desirableness.

enablement:
中：[计] 允许, 启动, 实现
英：n. The act of enabling, or the state of being enabled;
   ability.

enterography:
中：[医] 肠动描记法
英：n. A treatise upon, or description of, the intestines;
   enterology.

erst:
音标：/ә:st/
中：adv. 以前, 往昔的
英：r at a previous time;

euphemistical:
中：a. 委婉的, 婉言的
英：a. Pertaining to euphemism; containing a euphemism;
   softened in expression.

evolvement:
中：n. 展开, 进化, 发展, 进展
英：n. The act of evolving, or the state of being evolved;
   evolution.

exanthematous:
中：[医] 疹的, 发疹的
英：a. Of, relating to, or characterized by, exanthema;
   efflorescent; as, an exanthematous eruption.

excarnation:
中：[医] 修切标本
英：n. The act of depriving or divesting of flesh;
   excarnification; -- opposed to incarnation.

exfetation:
中：[医] 子宫外孕
英：n Imperfect fetation in some organ exterior to the uterus;
   extra-uterine fetation.

exorbitancy:
音标：/ɪɡ'zɔ:bɪtənsɪ/
中：n. 过度, 不当
英：n. A going out of or beyond the usual or due limit;
   hence, enormity; extravagance; gross deviation from rule, right, or
   propriety; as, the exorbitances of the tongue or of deportment;
   exorbitance of demands.

extravagantness:
中：n. extravagant的变形
英：n. The state of being extravagant or in excess;
   excess; extravagance.
